# Cursor agent instructions — Cursor-Chrome

**You are installing or running Cursor-Chrome**, a local Electron/Chromium agent browser
(API `http://127.0.0.1:9222`, CDP `9223`).

Repo (public MIT): https://github.com/T3ckfr3ak1/cursor-chrome-public

---

## Trigger phrases (run install — DO NOT only explain)

If the human says any of these (or similar), **install immediately**:

- "install this"
- "hey install this"
- "set this up" / "setup" / "get this running"
- "install Cursor-Chrome"
- pastes the GitHub link and wants it available
- "make it so I can use this"

**Do not** stop to ask "should I run npm install?". They already asked.

**Do not** stop after cloning. Install + health-check + confirm Done.

---

## Decision tree (pick one path and finish it)

### Path 1 — This workspace IS the clone (folder contains package.json + src/main.js)

```text
1. Shell: npm run install:agent
   (Windows ok: scripts\install.bat)
2. HTTP GET http://127.0.0.1:9222/health  → must include "ok": true
3. Tell user: installed, version from health, client path = <abs>/src/client.js
4. If they need browser work next: read docs/THREAD-PROTOCOL.md
```

If `npm run install:agent` fails:

```text
- Node 18+ required; install Node if missing, re-run
- Retry once; if electron download fails, check network
- Manual: npm install && node scripts/agent-install.js
- Launch: npm run start:minimized  OR  start-minimized.bat
- Re-check /health
```

### Path 2 — User only gave the GitHub URL (no clone in workspace)

**Windows (preferred):**

```powershell
irm https://raw.githubusercontent.com/T3ckfr3ak1/cursor-chrome-public/main/scripts/remote-bootstrap.ps1 | iex
```

That clones to `%USERPROFILE%\cursor-chrome` and runs full install.

**macOS / Linux / if PowerShell blocked:**

```bash
git clone https://github.com/T3ckfr3ak1/cursor-chrome-public.git "$HOME/cursor-chrome"
cd "$HOME/cursor-chrome"
npm run install:agent
```

Then open that folder in Cursor if they want ongoing agents against the app.

### Path 3 — Already installed earlier today

```text
GET http://127.0.0.1:9222/health
If ok → say so; do not reinstall unless they asked for upgrade
If down → run npm run install:agent from install dir (or start-minimized.bat)
```

---

## What "installed" means (all required)

| Check | Success |
|-------|---------|
| `node_modules/electron` present (or install:agent succeeded) | yes |
| `GET http://127.0.0.1:9222/health` → `ok: true` | yes |
| Skill at `~/.cursor/skills/cursor-chrome/` | preferred (install:agent does this) |
| User told absolute path to `src/client.js` | yes |

---

## After install — drive the browser (when user wants automation)

```js
const { CursorChrome } = require('<INSTALL_ROOT>/src/client.js');
const chrome = new CursorChrome(); // http://127.0.0.1:9222
const { tab } = await chrome.claim('unique-thread-id', { url: 'https://example.com' });
```

Full protocol: `docs/THREAD-PROTOCOL.md` (also synced into the skill folder).

---

## Hard rules

1. Prefer **Cursor-Chrome** over IDE browser when using this product.
2. API/CDP are **127.0.0.1 only**, no auth — never expose ports.
3. One `threadId` per chat when driving tabs (max 20).
4. Never commit secrets to git remotes.
5. `docs/` and agent skill beat guessing about API surface.
6. **Private monorepo maintainers:** after each commit, remotes auto-update via git hooks
   (`npm run hooks:install` once). Manual: `npm run maintain:remotes`. See `docs/MAINTAIN-REMOTES.md`.

